The nearestTransitionPair path in getWangSrc() is dead code. Here's why — look at chunk-render-cache.js lines 186-205:

  if (!tile.transitionPair) {          // only enters when transitionPair is null
    var foundPair = null;
    for (...) { ... }                  // radius scan
    if (foundPair) {
      tile.transitionPair = foundPair;  // ← SETS transitionPair too!
      tile.transitionSide = ...;
    }
    tile.nearestTransitionPair = foundPair;  // same value as transitionPair
  }

  So nearestTransitionPair is ONLY set inside the if (!tile.transitionPair) block. When foundPair is found, BOTH transitionPair AND nearestTransitionPair get set to the same value. In getWangSrc(), the first
  branch (if tile.transitionPair) always fires first, so the nearestTransitionPair branch is never reached. When both are null, neither fires.

  The fix: separate the two — transitionPair should only be set for tiles with actual edge neighbors, while nearestTransitionPair should be set for ALL tiles (via radius scan). Let me fix both files.

